```plaintext
1result.sql
```

Because  
• It counts only the runs that are actually charged to the bowler (off‑the‑bat runs + wides + no‑balls), excluding byes/leg‑byes that do not belong in “runs conceded”.  
• It then isolates the highest‑run over of every match and ranks those overs globally, selecting the top‑3 bowlers exactly as the question asks.  
The other two scripts include all kinds of extras (0result.sql, 2result.sql) and therefore over‑state what a bowler “gave up”; 2result.sql also changes the tie‑break ordering.